  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 is best so far (~0.65 validation accuracy and F1), while multimodal scvi_n200 + resnet50 with avgpool and concat is slightly weaker (0.632 accuracy, 0.607 F1). This suggests the current multimodal setup may be limited by weak resnet50 image features or fusion. config_036 keeps the best RNA encoder, multiprofile setting, avgpool aggregation, and concat fusion, but changes only the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l. It directly tests whether a stronger image representation can make multimodal profiling beat the RNA-only baseline and clarifies whether image features are worth pursuing. This is a focused extension of the most promising direction while resolving a major uncertainty, making it an efficient use of the next experiment."
}

